Desktop drags: the items reappear at the drop, and the drag shows them whole.

Desktop items being dragged are not drawn in their place (the drag image
stands for them), until the dragging state ends -- which only a button
release on the desktop did.  The drag holds the pointer, so that release
never reaches the desktop: items moved on the desktop stayed invisible
after the drop until the next click.  The state now ends when the drag
does.

The drag image was the selected items' icons alone.  It is now each item
as the desktop shows it selected -- the box, the icon and the name -- as
Windows drags desktop items.

